<title>ITALY: San Paolo sees cap gain from Crediop sale.</title>
<headline>San Paolo sees cap gain from Crediop sale.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian banking group San Paolo di Torino on Tuesday said that it would see a minimum capital gain of 130 billion lire on the 40 percent stake in Crediop it sold to Franco-Belgian bank group Dexia earlier this year.  </p>
<p>The stake sale was announced in a statement in February giving a price of between 480 and 565 billion lire. At the lower price of 480 billion lire, the capital gain would be 130 billion lire, San Paolo said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
